cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  MPSynth: Shallow Approximate Quantum State Preparation from Matrix
  Product States
message: >-
  If you use this software, or results produced with it, please cite it.
  If you cite a specific number, please say which one -- the CNOT-reduction
  figures are measured against Qiskit's own exact StatePreparation
  construction on eight named datasets, not a universal constant.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Egemen
    family-names: Sarıaslan
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-06'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/egemensariaslan/mpsynth'
abstract: >-
  MPSynth compresses an N-dimensional classical vector into a Matrix
  Product State, truncates its bond dimension to a user-chosen fidelity
  tolerance, and synthesises the result as a shallow stack of
  nearest-neighbour two-qubit staircases -- depth growing linearly in the
  qubit count rather than exponentially, as exact amplitude encoding
  requires. Every two-qubit gate is lowered to RZ/RY/CX by an exact Cartan
  (KAK) decomposition using the minimum CX count its coordinates allow.
  Circuits export to OpenQASM 2.0/3.0, QIR, Q#, PennyLane and Qiskit from
  one shared gate set. Measured against Qiskit's own exact
  StatePreparation construction, MPSynth uses 14.6x fewer CNOTs on
  average (95% CI +/-6.7) at 99.9% fidelity, with CNOT count scaling
  linearly in qubit count (R^2 = 0.982, n = 8 to 18).
notes: >-
  Capstone project for the Microsoft AI/ML Summer Internship Programme,
  2026. A capstone project produced during the programme; not affiliated
  with or endorsed by Microsoft Corporation.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - state preparation
  - matrix product states
  - tensor networks
  - amplitude encoding
  - quantum circuit synthesis
  - OpenQASM
